  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---\ntype: KnowLP document\nstatus: engine\ndate: \"2026-08-29\"\nnote: engine README (v3.0.8 repo edition, dsh-first)\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "KnowLP-RAG",
      "text": "**Agent-first knowledge retrieval** — turn your Markdown notes into a self-maintaining knowledge graph that is \"use it or lose it\". Agents (DSH / Claude Code) install, build the graph, and self-check it; only the vault path must be provided by the human. Retrieval returns reading paths: which notes to read, in what order, and which are similar substitutes.\n\n[](https://python.org)\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://dsh.directory/plugins/wly8691-jpg/knowlp-rag)\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start (3 steps)",
      "text": "All three steps are agent-runnable; only `KNOWLP_VAULT` (your notes directory) must be provided by the human.\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Install (official npm registry)",
      "text": "dsh plugin add \"@eqman00003/knowlp-rag\""
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Set the two required env vars (without them the dual-graph engine idles and only full-text search works)",
      "text": "export KNOWLP_VAULT=\"$HOME/Notes\"              # your Markdown notes directory\nexport KNOWLP_GRAPH_DIR=\"$HOME/.knowlp-dsh\"    # writable index directory"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Restart dsh web — the first search triggers Python env bootstrap (~30s, don't interrupt)",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use from any MCP client",
      "text": "A `.mcp.json` ships at the repo root — copy it next to your project (or into your host's config), then provide the two required env vars (`KNOWLP_VAULT`, `KNOWLP_GRAPH_DIR`; the file reads them via `${...}`, so setting them in your shell is enough).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"knowlp\": {\n      \"type\": \"stdio\",\n\nTwo optional env vars matter when your notes live outside a plain-vault setup:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use from any MCP client",
      "text": "- `KNOWLP_SKILL_INDEX` — path to a skill index (enables `skill_search`);\n- `HERMES_HOME` — **only** needed for the chroma skill index when your agent home is not `~/.hermes`; the chroma DB resolves to `$HERMES_HOME/skills/.chroma/chroma.sqlite3`.\n\nThe config shape is verified over stdio (initialize → `tools/list` → a real `knowlp_search`); any stdio MCP host works."
    },
    {
      "section": "Try the demo vault (no private data, no embedding model)",
      "text": "A 7-note bilingual demo vault ships with the repo. From clone to first search:\n\nPOSIX:\n\n```bash\npip install -e .\nexport KNOWLP_VAULT=\"$PWD/examples/demo-vault\"\nexport KNOWLP_GRAPH_DIR=\"$PWD/.demo-graph\"\npython build_graph.py && python -m vector_index --build\n\nWindows PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\npip install -e .\n$env:KNOWLP_VAULT = \"$PWD\\examples\\demo-vault\"\n$env:KNOWLP_GRAPH_DIR = \"$PWD\\.demo-graph\"\npython build_graph.py; python -m vector_index --build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Try the demo vault (no private data, no embedding model)",
      "text": "Five bilingual verification queries and what each demonstrates:\n[docs/demo.md](docs/demo.md). Agent onboarding instructions:\n[examples/agent-setup.md](examples/agent-setup.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Seven tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `knowlp_search` | Four-engine fan-out retrieval (dual-graph P/S-Agent + vector + full-text) |\n| `knowlp_get_note` | Read note content (read-only, path-traversal safe) |\n| `knowlp_stats` | Engine/graph health self-check (first stop for troubleshooting) |\n| `knowlp_status` | Index lifecycle status (missing/fresh/stale + reason + exact fix command) |\n| `knowlp_record_feedback` | Explicit feedback (the only entry point of the weight loop) |\n| `knowlp_record_correction` | Explicit preference pairs (chosen ≻ rejected) — the input to preference learning |\n| `skill_search` | Skill index retrieval |"
    },
    {
      "section": "PixelRAG (optional cross-machine visual retrieval)",
      "text": "PixelRAG is an optional **visual-retrieval** engine — it embeds visual content\nfor retrieval instead of relying on text tokens alone. It runs on a **separate\nGPU machine** on your network: the agent offloads the visual-embedding work to\nthat box over Tailscale rather than computing it on the laptop. Retrieval falls\nback through three tiers:"
    },
    {
      "section": "PixelRAG (optional cross-machine visual retrieval)",
      "text": "1. **desktop GPU** — the primary dedicated box (an RTX-class machine reachable over Tailscale)\n2. **local** — a same-machine fallback\n3. **cloud API** — a hosted PixelRAG endpoint\n\nConfigure it via `KNOWLP_PIXELRAG_DESKTOP` / `pixelrag_local`. Unconfigured, it stays off — retrieval still works in n-gram / embedding mode."
    },
    {
      "section": "PixelRAG (optional cross-machine visual retrieval)",
      "text": "> **Reproducing this**: it is deployment-specific — you need your own GPU machine running a PixelRAG service, a network path to it (e.g. Tailscale), and its endpoint address. No bundled service ships with KnowLP."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "- Install & usage guide: [docs/usage.md](docs/usage.md)\n- Troubleshooting: [docs/troubleshooting.md](docs/troubleshooting.md)\n- dsh integration details (env vars / Cordis plugin): [dsh/README.md](dsh/README.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why KnowLP?",
      "text": "Grep for \"RAG architecture\" gives you 105 files. KnowLP gives you 3 ranked hits with dependency context."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why KnowLP?",
      "text": "| | `grep` | Naive vector store | **KnowLP** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Result ranking | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Dependency chain (P-Agent) | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n| Similar substitutes (S-Agent) | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n| Works without GPU | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ (n-gram mode) |\n| Improves with use (feedback) | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ (weight loop) |\n| Paragraph-level matching | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n| Decay & forgetting (use it or lose it) | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ (three half-life tiers) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why KnowLP?",
      "text": "**The difference**: vector search finds documents that \"contain keywords\"; KnowLP finds documents you *should read given your query*, with reading paths. Edge weights between notes evolve with usage — consumed edges strengthen, unused edges decay by half-life (ephemeral 1 day / default 30 days / declarative never).\n\nWorks with Chinese note vaults out of the box (Chinese time-anchor queries and Chinese full-text search are supported)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "```\n$ knowlp_search \"RAG architecture\"\n  1. [HIT]  RAG Architecture.md (score 0.77)\n  2. [LINK] Vector Database Selection.md (score 0.61)     ← prerequisite chain\n  3. [LINK] Retrieval Eval Pitfalls.md (score 0.42)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Local development",
      "text": "```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/wly8691-jpg/knowlp-rag.git\ncd knowlp-rag\npip install -e .            # provides knowlp-mcp / knowlp-build / knowlp-search"
    },
    {
      "section": "configure vault in config.yaml → build graph → search",
      "text": "python build_graph.py\npython knowlp_search.py \"RAG architecture\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\npip install -e \".[mcp,modeling]\" pytest pypdf\npython -m pytest -q\n```\n\nNothing in the suite needs a GPU, a real Office install, or a private vault, so\n**CI runs all of it** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, on every push and PR)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "| Layer | What it covers | In CI |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/test_packaging_closure.py` | The two manifests against the real import graph: **every** top-level module is covered, and everything the MCP entry can reach is in npm `files`. A deliberately empty `files` entry turns it red and names the importers. | yes |\n| the rest of `tests/` | Retrieval and routing, dual graph, modality pools, the preference loop, evidence/result contracts, and a real MCP stdio integration test. | yes |\n| the skips | Four need symlink privileges (developer mode on Windows). The fifth — the real-vault parity case — only runs when `KNOWLP_VAULT` points at a real vault. | — |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "Against a real vault locally: `303 passed, 4 skipped`. On CI, where the vault is\ndeliberately unreachable: `302 passed, 5 skipped`. The one test difference is the\nreal-vault parity case, and it says so in the skip reason.\n\n`test_packaging_closure.py` exists because 3.0.10 shipped without it: the npm\ntarball was missing 16 top-level modules, six of them in the MCP entry's import\nclosure, and `knowlp_search` could not run at all from an npm install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "[View Architecture Diagram](https://wly8691-jpg.github.io/knowlp-rag/architecture.html)"
    }
